AND WHEREAS, it is expedient to prohibit https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Gutkha and Panmasala in the State of Tamil Nadu, being food products in which tobacco and nicotine are widely used as ingredients;
AND WHEREAS, consumption of the above such products will endanger human health and well being and whereas, if consumption of these food articles is allowed without prohibition the well being of current and future generation will be compromised and hence it has to be prohibited.
The Hon'ble Supreme Court of India in Central ARECANUT Marketing Corporation and Others Vs. Union Of India (Transfer case (c) 1 of 2010) in its order dated 23-09-2016 observed that to circumvent the ban on the sale of Gutkha, the manufacturers are selling panmasala (without tobacco) with flavoured chewing tobacco in separate sachets but often conjoint and sold together by the same vendors from the same premises.
